{
  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "items": [
        "Clients keep a local copy plus a queue of unacknowledged ops, so typing and dragging never wait on the network",
        "On reconnect, pending ops are replayed / re-transformed / re-merged \u2014 never silently discarded"
      ],
      "title": "Local-first clients"
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "items": [
        "A central server per document transforms incoming ops (OT) or merges commutative updates (CRDT), then broadcasts",
        "Full peer-to-peer sync adds complexity most products don't need, since edits already flow through servers"
      ],
      "title": "Server as arbiter"
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "items": [
        "OT is battle-tested for linear text (Google Docs); CRDTs generalize to trees (Figma: last-write-wins per property)",
        "CRDT tombstones grow unbounded \u2014 periodic snapshot + bounded history (Figma: ~7 days) cuts file size ~90%"
      ],
      "title": "OT vs CRDT & growth"
    }
  ],
